BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Live/Free] SF’s Free “Pop-Ups on the Plaza”: Celebrating La
 tine Makers (Ferry Plaza)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T210000
DTSTAMP:20260930T214945Z
UID:funcheap-20261003-sfsfreepopupsontheplazac
CATEGORIES:concert,free
DESCRIPTION:https://sf.funcheap.com/popups-plaza-celebrating-latine-makers
 -sfs-ferry-building/\nLocation: south bay\nPrice: Free\nCategories: concer
 t\, free\nSource: funcheap/south-bay\n\nThis Hispanic History Month\, cele
 brate Bay Area Latine makers with a day of delicious food\, crafts\, and c
 ommunity at the Embarcadero Ferry Terminal Plaza (south of the Ferry Build
 ing) and Ferry Plaza Farmers Market. Entry is free and open to the public\
 , and food and drinks will be available for purchase. Pop-Ups on the Plaza
 : Celebrating Latine Makers Saturday\, October 3\, 2026 | 9a-2p Embarcader
 o Ferry Terminal Plaza (south of Ferry Building) FREE Pop-Ups on the Plaza
  is a series of events celebrating Bay Area BIPOC entrepreneurs\, includin
 g businesses in Foodwise’s Building Equity program. Pop-Ups on the Plaza
  is a Port sponsored event brought to you by Foodwise. This program is pro
 udly funded in partnership with the San Francisco Human Rights Commission.
  Additional support is provided by the Ferry Building. View this post on I
 nstagram A post shared by Foodwise (@foodwise) Participating Vendors Agua 
 Frisco : Locally made artisan agua frescas Chi Chi’s Kiosko : Empanadas\
 , Puerto Rican sandwich combos\, and passion fruit juice Clandestina Cocin
 a : Cuban rice bowls (lechon\, roasted chicken\, or ropa vieja)\, Cuban sa
 ndwiches\, guava and cheese turnovers\, and guava limeade Dulce Maná : Co
 l
LOCATION:south bay
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/popups-plaza-celebrating-latine-makers-sfs-fer
 ry-building/
END:VEVENT
