 y Children’s Halloween Haunt takes over History Park with hayrides\, car
 nival games\, a mini pumpkin patch\, cultural fall crafts\, and trick-or-t
 reating at the site’s historic house museums. The program also includes 
 an optional Sugar Skull workshop led by Elizabeth McCarthy and concludes w
 ith a 6:00 PM light show. History Park is located at the south end of Kell
 ey Park at the corner of Senter Road and Phelan Avenue. Through original a
 nd reproduction homes\, businesses\, and landmarks\, History Park reveals 
 Santa Clara Valley’s past. Complete with paved streets\, running trolley
 s\, and an old-fashioned ice parlor\, this 14-acre site offers the charm a
 nd ambiance of times gone by. Address : 635 Phelan Ave. San Jose\, CA 9511
